{"title":"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Greater_detail_and_more_straightforward)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Greater detail and more straightforward)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7400e866ec206aeeca3f416d787b8bbeed9e1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with real coefficients, nonzero constant term, and no repeated roots. Suppose that for any real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c9fcfb0bca83ce1b069481930e7d18723dc87e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, \\dots, a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" /> such that the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/e/48e62d7addb7049530e9be2c26abb6a6fbd16590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_kx^k+\\cdots+a_1x+a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b956769dee0aab3260aa7708dd91d3e8dddf497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0a_1\\cdots a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> is zero. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> has a nonreal root.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed by contradiction. Assume that all roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> are real. Let the distinct roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2aff5975895bdfe4500899889b436976c63c69bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\ldots, r_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" />, all nonzero since the constant term is nonzero.\n</p><p>Consider any subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a542075244cf88feaa6cc1d84176fd61fd57cd43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{r_{i_1}, r_{i_2}, \\ldots, r_{i_k}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> and form the polynomial:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2141968123f687e13045129703ad17d8c89d30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(x) = \\prod_{j=1}^k (x - r_{i_j}) =a_{k} x^k + a_{k-1}x^{k-1} + \\cdots + a_0\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>By Vieta's formulas:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/9475ff2171601c7112541fe326e907a934f0c9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = (-1)^k \\prod_{j=1}^k r_{i_j} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"171\" height=\"58\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b0bad88bc9e35b6828a83ec12ae01505ac50a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1} = -\\sum_{j=1}^k r_{i_j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"127\" height=\"58\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/52754e22f6491eacdf6f44e9963f407d38303063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-2} = \\sum_{1\\leq m&lt;n\\leq k} r_{i_m}r_{i_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"176\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe given condition requires that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace148188777577c624b8d69e1450a4114aa2533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0a_1\\cdots a_k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026d01d3f2600a7e756cb88c0a4e32d752279c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, at least one other coefficient must be zero.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\nFor any pair of roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b409f2636794495eadf4eafca866071648fc2c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r_i, r_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af0f31e4addf9550395101da43afa3d12f5969.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(x) = x^2 - (r_i+r_j)x + r_ir_j\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" />\nThe condition implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a82254bd55b505520c2c5c524ea339393e4a345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-r_ir_j(r_i+r_j) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61cf6a44a40aaf1c548f335876ca29d87b712ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i + r_j = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"86\" height=\"19\" /> for all pairs. But with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, considering three roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2b055c89a98960f69ada4b7990044d435b27b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"11\" /> gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c237efaff6d1e1faf52f83350315d0378c5c8013.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_1 + r_2 = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad r_1 + r_3 = 0 \\implies r_2 = r_3\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"15\" />\ncontradicting distinct roots.\nIn General:\nFor any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> roots, some symmetric sum must be zero. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, this would require:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/7/5c77288f7998b7ae88e42f738e5277b8783b0ff3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_i + r_j + r_m = 0 \\quad \\text{for all triples}\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"17\" />\nwhich leads to contradictions for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/83870118206bd0e612b5c9e3def2ef95460e368b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> as it would force roots to be equal.\n</p><p>Thus, our initial assumption is false, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must have at least one nonreal root.~Jonathan\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Greater_detail_and_more_straightforward.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Greater_detail_and_more_straightforward)\">Solution 2 (Greater detail and more straightforward)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Greater detail and more straightforward)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the sake of contradiction, assume all roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> are real. Then, there exists a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> whose roots are subsets of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and one of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is 0.\n</p><p>Indeed, if distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b0ce37cd40182a281d2bc84216ba2dfd0ce467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\dots, r_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"11\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, some subset of these roots satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f226dec7637fd3181d293c2ddb8114f4bcd672ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-r_{i_1})(x- r_{i_2})(\\dots)(x-r_{i_k}) = a_{k} x^k + a_{k-1}x^{k-1} + \\cdots + a_0\\]\" width=\"473\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d9674015097f7236214f3fa291aa57dbd61c754f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> by method of undetermined coefficients. In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026d01d3f2600a7e756cb88c0a4e32d752279c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> by the nonzero constant given in the statement. That implies some other term is 0.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc028050428615cc28ee3c1f9a67eda8e9a726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> denote the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-th symmetric summation. It follows that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d85d157c80485667f4d2c5342394e194ff79ed7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{k-1} = -s_1\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"11\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e815b3d2ece0de472e5946b8b0f19b914ef7f434.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{k-2} = s_2\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"11\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16762e47f22f53e2431935f211fa82570b46b6cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c2dd38dd1a3c1ffe8aae0b74fd832bffa564b56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_0 = (-1)^k s_k \\neq 0 \\implies s_k \\neq 0\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>However, that last claim implies one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb313e4e3cf28b59a295a5e4674e146de6f9fa59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1, s_2, s_3, \\dots, s_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" /> is 0, which then implies, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0950c6ab987e57b2b8d030db0f79acc376c129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k = r_{i_1} r_{i_2} \\dots r_{i_k} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />, none of the roots equal 0. However, notice that then if any one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c07baec67f7a526d293aa37c287a569025595ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_p \\ : \\ p \\leq k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" /> must equal 0.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even, we can rewrite some of the symmetric sums by groups. For one of these to equal 0, it follows that some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd607e68b4fbc97745ee3f5a8ff597589ce4bc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n}{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"41\" height=\"55\" /> of the groups formed, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />th symmetric sum, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of roots, has the property exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/939118fe858ff026108742a23de78e890fc389a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\binom{n}{i}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" /> of the sums of elements are direct opposites of the others. However, one quickly realizes that if all terms are relatively prime, it is forced at least one of the roots given is 0, which is a contradiction, or if they are not relatively prime, one can divide by the greatest common factor and obtain some root sequence that is indeed relatively prime, which either forces at least one of the roots to be 0 or two roots to equal one another, both of which are contradictions.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd however, this implies one of the roots must equivalate to 0 by the Zero Product Property, a contradiction.\n</p><p>Because no such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> exists, no such subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> roots can exist, and therefore no such polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> can exist, which implies no such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> can exist, and therefore it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> has at least one nonreal root, and so the proof is complete. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO\" title=\"2025 USAMO\">2025 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017154847\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 376/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11985/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.966      1 -total\n 57.23%    6.848      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.96%    4.901      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31349:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017154847 and revision id 290428. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}